cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Tab Order Visualizer"
abstract: >-
  A browser tool that visualizes the keyboard tab order of any web page and flags
  focus-related accessibility problems: focus order jumps (WCAG 2.4.3), focusable
  elements that are not visible (WCAG 2.4.7), clickable elements that cannot be
  reached with the keyboard (WCAG 2.1.1) and missing focus indicators (WCAG 2.4.7).
  It computes sequential focus navigation order following the HTML specification,
  including shadow DOM, slots, radio groups and positive tabindex, and exports
  findings as HTML, CSV or Markdown reports.
type: software
